      "rationale": "The specification declares the country of origin for both the product and its primary ingredient (Joghurt/MILCH, 82%) as 'Deutschland'. According to Art. 26(2), the origin must be given if omitting it could mislead the consumer, and Art. 26(3) requires that if the origin of the food is given and differs from the primary ingredient, this must be stated. Here, both origins are the same and are declared, so the requirement is satisfied.",
